include "../compiler/runtime/elisacore_std/elisacore_runtime.elisa"

# stage1 takes EXPONENTIAL time on a long field-access chain. stage0 rejects the
# same input immediately.
#
# Measured, stage1 -emit obj, chain length vs wall clock:
#
#     links   time        links   time
#         5     21 ms        20      66 ms
#        10     16 ms        22     208 ms
#        15     18 ms        25    1715 ms
#        18     29 ms
#
# ~1.75x per additional link. The oracle's own `chain.elisa` has 400 links, which
# extrapolates to ~2e91 seconds -- not a hang in the deadlock sense, just a
# complete algorithmic blowup. stage0 on the same file: rc=1 in well under a
# second (it reports 400 errors and stops).
#
# THIS BLOCKS test/parity/semantic_internal_diff.sh. That check feeds ~3.3k oracle
# sources through build/parse_report, which embeds stage1's frontend; row 726
# (chain.elisa) never returns, so the gate's longest check can never finish. It
# was observed burning 94 minutes of CPU at 100% with FLAT 1.3 MB RSS.
#
# NOT caused by the compiler work in this session. The failing path is field-chain
# resolution; nothing in the const/escape/extern/target-predefine changes touches
# it, and the blowup is visible at 25 links in a file with no consts, no escapes
# and no externs. It became REACHABLE only because fixing the stage0 sview crash
# (SESSION_COMPILER_FIXES.md #3) let parse_report build at all -- before that this
# check died at tool-build time and never ran a single row.
#
# THE TRIGGER IS ERROR RECOVERY, not field access. A chain on a type that HAS the
# field resolves fine on both stages (a `struct Node: b: Node&` version of this
# compiles in 2.2s on stage1 vs 1.5s on stage0 -- a 1.5x difference, not a
# blowup). The pathological case is a chain on a type with NO such field, where
# every link fails to resolve and the recovery path re-explores the prefix.
#
# `a` is an i64 and i64 has no field `b`, so all 25 links are errors -- exactly
# what the oracle's chain.elisa does with 400 of them.
#
# Raise the chain length to taste: 22 links ~0.2s, 25 ~1.7s, 30 ~25s.

def f(a: i64) -> i64:
    return a.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b.b

def main() -> i64:
    return 0
